            <ArticleTitle>Improved exercise myocardial perfusion during lidoflazine therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>705-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lidoflazine is a synthetic drug with calcium-channel blocking effects. In a study of 6 patients with severe classic angina pectoris, single-blind administration of lidoflazine was associated with improved myocardial perfusion during exercise as determined by thallium-201 stress scintigraphy. These studies demonstrate that lidoflazine therapy is associated with relief of angina, an increased physical work capacity, and improved regional myocardial perfusion during exercise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
